<p>Central Texas homes are built for heat, not for days of hard freeze. Plumbing often runs through attics, exterior walls, and slab penetrations with little insulation, which works fine most winters and fails badly in a storm like Uri. When a pipe splits, water can run for hours before anyone notices, soaking drywall, flooring, cabinets, and insulation. This article explains how freeze damage and burst pipe insurance claims work in San Marcos: what recent winter storms did here, how policies treat frozen pipes, the clauses that cause the most disputes, and how to protect your claim from the first hour.</p>

